================================================================
DATASET
================================================================

Target: 10M+ positions with WDL labels drawn from self-play at
mid TC (10+0.1) using shaybot_pass4 binary.

Position filter (standard quiet criteria):
  - Side to move is not in check
  - Last move was not a capture or pawn push
  - Ply >= 8 (discard opening book plies)
  - Eval within reasonable window (e.g. |eval| < 1000cp) to
    avoid skewing on already-decided positions

At ~30 qualifying plies per game this yields ~200k positions
per 10k games; 500k games required for 10M positions.

Supplement with a standard quiet-labeled EPD (Zurichess, CCRL
quiet, or Ethereal dataset) to improve coverage of:
  - Pawn weakness structures (batch 4 bias correction)
  - Endgame outpost positions (batch 8b signal failure)
  - Passed pawn endgames (batch 5 signal failure)
These are genuinely underrepresented in opening-book self-play
games at any TC, and no amount of self-play volume fixes it.

Tune K (sigmoid scaling constant) first on a held-out 500k
subset before running any parameter optimization. Fix K for
all subsequent steps.

