================================================================
TUNING ORDER
================================================================

Step 1 – K calibration
  Tune K on held-out 500k subset. Fix K for all steps.

Step 2 – Piece values + all 12 PSTs simultaneously
  Highest-leverage step. Expect significant movement: piece
  values may shift 10-30 points, PST corner/edge values may
  swing large. Do not proceed until this stabilizes.

Step 3 – Batches 3, 6, 7, 8a simultaneously
  Reasonable SPSA warm starts; expect smaller deltas than step 2.

Step 4 – Batch 4 (pawn structure) + Batch 5 (passed pawns)
  Run separately because pawn terms interact strongly with
  Pawn_PST (fixed from step 2). Enforce passed pawn
  monotonicity constraint throughout.

Step 5 – Batch 8b (outposts)
  Low cross-parameter interaction; can run jointly with step 4.

Step 6 – Full joint re-tune (all eval params, one final pass)
  Resolves cross-parameter compensation from sequential tuning.
  Expect small (<5 point) movements. Optional but recommended.

If using gradient-based optimizer (Adam/SGD) over the full
parameter vector simultaneously, steps 2-6 collapse into a
single run. This is preferred if implementation supports it.

================================================================
VERIFICATION GATE
================================================================

After each step:
  1. MSE on held-out 500k: must decrease monotonically.
     Any increase signals overfitting; reduce learning rate
     or check dataset imbalance (too few endgame positions).
  2. 400-game match vs shaybot_pass4 at 30+0.3 after each step.
     Expect monotone elo improvement. Regression > 10 elo flags
     that step's parameter group for investigation.
  3. After step 2 sanity checks:
       - Queen > 2*Rook + Pawn implied value
       - Bishop_Pair_Bonus (SPSA 22) + implied PST correction >= 26
       - King_PST_MG: e1/d1 squares are most negative on board
       - King_PST_EG: e4/d4/d5/e5 squares are most positive
  4. After step 4:
       - Isolated_MG more negative than Isolated_EG
       - Pawn_Center_EG and Pawn_ExtCenter_MG nonzero confirms
         dataset bias has been corrected by quiet supplement
       - Backward_EG nonzero (was 0 in SPSA)
  5. Final binary: texelpass1 vs shaybot_pass4 at 30+0.3
     (800 games). Expect substantial elo gain from PST and
     piece value tuning alone. If not, check for compensation
     artifacts (large PST + piece value shifts that cancel).

================================================================
POST-TEXEL: FINAL CMA-ES (SEARCH ONLY)
================================================================

After texelpass1 converges and the final binary is validated,
run one CMA-ES pass on the batch 1 + batch 2 search parameters.
Rationale: search optima are eval-dependent. With PSTs and piece
values now properly set, LMR/FP/history optima may shift.

Expected shift: small (5-15 units) for most params. LMR_Base
and LMR_Scale are most likely to move as they interact with
eval quality at quiescence cutoffs.

Parameters to re-tune:
  LMR_Base, LMR_Scale, FP_Mult, FP_Base, SE_Margin, RFP_Margin,
  ASP_Delta, SEE_Pruning_Margin, SE_Reduction_Denom,
  History_Bonus_Mult, History_Bonus_Sub, History_Bonus_Limit,
  Main_History_Weight, CMH_Weight, FMH_Weight.

Use top-10% centroid metric for all final value selection.
Minimum TC 10+0.1; prefer 30+0.3 for this final pass.